{comment: Intro}
[G]  [A]  [D/F#]  [G]

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]My hope is built on nothing [A]less
[Em]Than Jesus' blood and [G]righteousness
[G]I dare not trust the sweetest [A]frame
[Em]But wholly lean on Jesus' [G]name

{comment: Chorus}
[D]On Christ the solid rock I [Em7]stand
[D/F#]All other ground is [G]sinking [A]sand
[Bm]All other ground is [A]sinking [G]sand

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]When darkness seems to hide his [A]face
[Em]I rest on his unchanging [G]grace
[G]In every high and stormy [A]gale
[Em]My anchor holds within the [G]veil

{comment: Chorus}

{comment: Verse 3}
[G]His oath, His covenant, His [A]blood
[Em]Support me in the whelming [G]flood
[G]When all around my soul gives [A]way
[Em]He then is all my hope and [G]stay

{comment: Chorus}

{comment: Verse 4 (Alt last verse)}
[D]When He shall come with trumpet [Dsus4]sound
[A]Oh may I then in Him be [D]found
[D]Dressed in His righteousness a[Dsus4]lone
[A]Faultless to stand before the [D]throne

{comment: Chorus}


